   "id": "dishes_baked",
   "text": "Two frozen dishes are inside the refrigerator (the tall white appliance between the sink counter and the black built-in oven): a fish casserole in the round baking dish and a lasagna in the rectangular baking dish. Each must first be thawed in the microwave on the west preparation counter and then baked in the black built-in oven to the right of the refrigerator; a dish that is still frozen does not bake in the oven. The fish casserole thaws in about 6 minutes and then bakes in about 4 minutes; the lasagna thaws in about 2 minutes and then bakes in about 10 minutes. Thawing and baking only progress while the appliance door is closed and the appliance is switched on. The microwave takes only one baking dish at a time and switches itself off when it is done; the oven holds both dishes at once and does not switch itself off.",
